&gt;&gt;=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 # Relaxing a MUST in the base TLS spec?=
<br>
&gt;&gt; <br>
&gt;&gt;=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 CURRENT:<br>
&gt;&gt;=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0[TLS13] requires that ``Th=
e key_exchange values for each<br>
&gt;&gt;=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0KeyShareEntry MUST be gene=
rated independently.&#39;&#39; In the context of<br>
&gt;&gt;=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0this document, since the s=
ame algorithm may appear in multiple named<br>
&gt;&gt;=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0groups, this document rela=
xes the above requirement to allow the same<br>
&gt;&gt;=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0key_exchange value for the=
 same algorithm to be reused in multiple<br>
&gt;&gt;=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0KeyShareEntry records sent=
 in within the same ClientHello.<br>
&gt;&gt; <br>
&gt;&gt;=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 Isn=E2=80=99t this modifying aspects of=
 the base TLS? How to reconcile this with the<br>
&gt;&gt;=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 claim in the previous point?<br>
&gt;&gt; <br>
&gt;&gt; <br>
